<p>To achieve this, we can start by advancing the leader pointer through th=
e linked list for k steps. When the leader pointer is k nodes ahead of the =
trailer, we can advance both pointers together until the leader reaches the=
 last node. This process will be explained in more detail soon.</p>
<p>However, there=E2=80=99s an important edge case to consider first: <stro=
ng>what if the head itself is the node we need to remove?</strong> In this =
case, there=E2=80=99s no node before the head, so we cannot perform the rem=
oval, as mentioned earlier. To circumvent this, we can create a <code>dummy=
